WEBVTT

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.150
Yeah! Right there! Get him!

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.450
Hey, where are you going? No chickening out!

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.410
Oh, my...

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.750
Hey, Kosaku! You've got yourself one hell of a punch!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.250
Yeah, that was really something!

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.080
Hey, ref! He's down! Give him the count already! {I merged them since they were bad with split - ninja}

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.290
U-Uh, right... I'll get to it, then.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.720
Dammit, not one of these bastards is worth a damn!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.350
Can't any of you guys give 'em an enthusiastic fight like Joe once in a while?

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.810
That'll draw some more customers, for sure!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.520
I wouldn't call that fair, Kono-san.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:12.520
Ever since Joe joined, he's beat the snot out of all of us.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.320
Yeah, that's right!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.530
I've had enough of getting my ass kicked!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.320
Just take a look at what he did to our faces.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.530
We were all better off without Joe!

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:21.870
Yeah!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:22.620
He's right!

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.660
You gotta do something about this, Kono-san!

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.670
Well, uh... guys...

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:32.880
What I'm saying is, with Yabuki-kun fighting with Local Entertainment, we draw more customers!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.550
And that'll result in your income being doubled or tripled-

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.550
<i>That's enough!</i>

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.140
You're asking the impossible.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.970
You see, Joe's not like the rest of us.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.680
Joe can't go on fighting trash boxers like us forever.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.570
He has to face an amazing rival worthy of him.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.690
The sooner the better.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.240
I'm talking about a real rival.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.230
Hey, Carlos!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.400
Yohko-san wants to talk to you.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.440
Okay.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.270
Come in.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.430
Hello, Miss Yohko.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.850
How are you today?

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.230
How is your training going, Carlos?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.040
My training? No need to worry, it's all good.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.070
I'm ready to enter the ring any time.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.990
How did the negotiations with Nango go, Miss?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.990
Everything's okay. He's signed the contract.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.210
And when's the match?

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.790
Next Sunday.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.670
So, it's finally time.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.960
Hey, Carlos!

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.340
Come over here!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.590
We need to talk to you!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.800
It's fine, Robert.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.340
I can hear you from here.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.130
Please, do continue.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.060
Now, the biggest problem was the venue.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.520
But Nango felt that a remote city would bring in more spectators,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.480
which is exactly what we wanted.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.100
I see. Which would mean...

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.110
Sendai, in Miyagi Prefecture?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.820
Yes. The Sendai Sports Center.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:06.110
Just a stone's throw from the troupe Yabuki Joe is touring with.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:13.120
Which means... Carlos, the rest is up to you.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.470
<i>{Muy Bien}</i>All right, I understand.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.930
My role is to stoop to being a touring boxer

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.510
to awaken Joe Yabuki from his leisurely life.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.140
That was it, right? Understood, don't worry.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.520
I'm not worried, Carlos.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:38.150
I just don't want you to forget that my goal is for you to fight Joe in the end.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.280
Yabuki, Yabuki.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.250
Yabuki, Yabuki! It's always Yabuki with you, Miss!

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.200
What is it with this Yabuki guy?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.670
What is it with Yabuki Joe?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.210
I don't even know myself.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:15.770
Whatever the case, you brought us all the way here from Venezuela to fight Yabuki Joe.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.060
So we will do everything we can to accomplish that goal.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:19.650
Now we'd best be off.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.150
Come on, Carlos. Let's go.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.790
<i>What is it with Yabuki Joe?</i>

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.540
<i>I don't even know myself.</i>

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.460
All I can say now is that he's lying dormant.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:49.300
And when he meets the Boxer of Terror known as Carlos Rivera,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.470
he will surely... surely awaken!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.940
Where are we going, Robert?

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:08.900
Carlos, not even I know why Yohko-san is so obsessed with Yabuki.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:15.700
But I looked into Yabuki, and found this out:

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.330
He is a boxer of unfathomable horror.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.330
Now you're going on about Yabuki too, Robert?

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:29.300
Right, I forgot that you don't judge things by words or emotions.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.810
Never mind. Just follow me and you might understand Joe Yabuki a little more.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.140
Driver, take us to San'ya in Asakusa.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.000
I-It's a slum! A Japanese slum!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.960
That's right. Venezuela's not the only place with slums.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.260
Robert! Why did you take me here? Huh!?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.050
Oh, right. You hate the slums.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.350
But I'm more fond of them.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:17.720
It was where I was born and raised, and where I met you.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.770
And this is Joe Yabuki's hometown.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.610
Joe Yabuki's...?

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.960
Hey!<i>{¿Como te llamas?}</i> What's your name?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.640
We've got a crisis on our hands!

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.110
What's that? A duo of suspicious-looking foreigners?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.200
Well, they looked suspicious <i>because</i> they were foreigners!

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:22.420
Oh, please. How can we live here in Japan if we're afraid of foreigners?

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.800
And they were nicely dressed, too.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:34.130
So, they look like they're loaded, huh?

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.350
Of course, of course!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.480
H-Hey, guys! They're right over the fence! What do we do?

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.240
Do you even have to ask?

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.650
You get out there and hustle 'em!

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.860
What, me?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.740
Of course, you! They're your marks!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.920
Hey, Mister!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.500
Come on, come on, stop!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.420
<i>Uh, thank you! Uh, blah blah blah, ramen, schmamen!</i>

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.930
Hey, guys, it's no good! Let's forget it!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.560
These foreigners don't speak a word of English!

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:23.270
They must be soft or something!

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.310
<i>We speak Japanese, you know.</i>

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.890
God!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.030
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.730
<i>That's enough outta you!</i>

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:42.660
I see, I see. So, you know Japanese, huh? 
That makes it easier.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.330
Yo. What brings ya all the way here?

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.830
Actually, I was hoping to see Tange Danpei-san.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.510
You mean Old Man Danpei?

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:55.050
Hey, I think this guy knows the old man!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.880
Sounds like the old man's become a little cosmopolitan!

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.760
What're you talking about? Hurry up and rip 'em off!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.930
Oh, right.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.930
We know where the old man is.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.200
Oh, that'll be a big help!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.440
Would you kindly show us to him?

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:11.440
Here.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.110
Just as a show of gratitude.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.150
We're busy people, you see.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.150
Oh, thanks.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:21.580
H-H-Hey, this is five thousand yen!

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:23.620
Oh my...

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.620
Wh-What's the matter? Is that not enough?

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.210
N-No, it's fine!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.370
Let's all show him the way!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.080
Yeah!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.350
Right this way!

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:53.520
See?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.030
Now this is a shame. He's plastered.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.490
Well, this is just what he's like without Bro Joe here.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.030
God damn it! God damn it!

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:49.910
That son of a bitch!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:53.170
Damn idiot!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:12:59.920
Those eyes...

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:09.100
The hell? You're not Joe.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.570
Figures. He wouldn't come back.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.860
He had the eyes of a beast. 
And that's what's wrong with him.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:25.990
I should never have believed he'd go anywhere when I saw his eyes.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.660
Real eyes of a boxer, huh?

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.920
Once a guy with those eyes gets caught up in fighting, he's doomed.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:40.590
Either he has to become the champion, or die like a dog in the ring.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.760
I've done a horrible thing.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.680
If only he'd never met me...

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.910
How long are you gonna keep on crying, old man?

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:12.030
Crying's not gonna bring Joe back.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:15.960
We're all holding out and waiting for him.

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:20.840
We know that Joe's gonna come back once he's stronger!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.720
Pardon me for a moment.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.810
Joe!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.510
Here's a pillow.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.350
Okay.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.970
Hey, Mister...

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.930
I'm giving this back.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.480
Oh, why?

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:25.150
I feel really bad about you having to help us bring this old drunk here.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.570
No, no! I don't need it!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.030
Keep it!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.150
Consider it cigarette money!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.540
Cig-?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.790
Okay, goodbye!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.540
Good work, mister!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.460
Bye!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.390
What's the matter, Carlos?

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.970
Joe Yabuki... what an idiot<i>{pendejo}</i>.{the one place gratuitous spanish works}

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.020
He left on a journey, even though he was loved by so many.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.070
Shouldn't you understand that best, Carlos?

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:09.070
I'm sure Joe Yabuki poured out his sweat and blood

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:15.330
and overcame countless problems here in this worn-down shack, before he understood

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.210
that what a boxer needs is not love, but solitude.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:21.960
The most solitude that he can have.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:24.960
That's why he left.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.960
He may just be the true boxer we've been looking for!

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:33.760
Joe Yabuki... I wish I could see him once more.

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:33.860
I gotta say, these guys have come a long way since Joe showed up.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:39.080
They've stopped staying up late and started training every morning!

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:41.980
Let's go!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:42.580
Right!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.210
H-Hey, wait! Wait!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.590
Hey, wait!

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.990
Nango... That's the last guy to knock me out!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.200
And it's in Sendai...

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.820
Now, that's just awful!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.830
Sendai Sports Center is just a stone's throw from us!

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:26.880
And they've got a world-ranked boxer
 and a Japanese main-eventer!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:32.840
Did the city ring really have to come all the way up here and steal our crowd?{alt "big-city boxing"}

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:35.840
Damn it, I'm so unlucky!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.840
The city ring, huh...

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.410
Robert, where did Carlos go?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.370
He went out into town.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.910
What? We just got into town, and he's already sightseeing?

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.500
Yeah. He told me he was going for a stroll,

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.910
but I bet he's hyped.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.590
Considering the fact that Yabuki's in this town.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.770
Hey, Joe!

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.860
Where are you going in this heat?

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.900
Nowhere special. Just gonna wander that way.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.200
Wander?

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.180
What's the matter, Nango?

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.190
You seem real stiff!

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.520
No, Coach. Nothing's wrong.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.440
It's all right! You <i>are</i> facing the sixth-ranked boxer in the world, after all.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:20.490
But Nango, don't forget the possibility that the rest of the world's lost its edge.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.870
Y-Yes, of course!

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.490
Sir, we can't have you here!

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:27.490
There's a match tomorrow! We can't have any unauthorized entry!

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.370
What's the matter? I'm just here for a little look around.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.370
I'd like to see a real ring for once.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:37.590
Well, you sure have got a good venue set up here, huh?

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:40.340
It's a world apart from a temple or shrine ground!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.720
Damn right.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.380
It can't be compared to a touring ring at all.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:49.270
Hey, Nango! Long time no see!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:50.490
Whoa, there!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.320
Who was that guy, Nango?

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:57.860
Oh, him?

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.330
I think his name was Yabuki.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.240
Some second-rate boxer who's been touring the sticks

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.580
ever since I knocked him out with my killer punch.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.790
Oh, him? And now he's buddying up to you?

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.780
That asshole...

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.410
Hold it, Nango!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.580
Let me show you how a second-rate boxer can punch!

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:22.590
Son of a...

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.300
Bastard!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.260
Goddammit!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.430
Come on! Is that all you got?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:31.180
<i>He's taking out my men! Get him, boys!</i>

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.360
Damn. Looks like this is getting bigger than I thought.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.110
You think you can pick a fight with us, you punk?

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.360
Let's pack him up and throw him into the office!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.120
Hold it!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.700
Freeze!

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.000
Damn it!

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:01.590
Get back here!

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:06.260
I knew I'd find you here, Joe Yabuki!

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:07.930
Wh-Who are you?

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:10.090
Carlos Rivera!

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:16.230
Carlos Rivera?

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.530
Not half bad!

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:56.310
Carlos Rivera... The world-ranked boxer called in by Shiraki Gym.

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:00.270
I've come to give you a little gift.

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:01.740
A gift?

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:04.860
Yes. It's something for your eyes only...

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.780
The secret weapon I'm gonna use against Nango.

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:09.780
Secret weapon?

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:14.780
If you're the man I think you are,

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:17.750
you should be able to see past my secret weapon.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:21.790
<i>{Buena suerte}</i>Good luck, Joe.

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:26.470
The world's sixth-ranked bantamweight...

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:28.340
Carlos Rivera...

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.760
I could feel it just by looking into his eyes...

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.940
Wh-What is this terror?

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.170
The bell has rung for the Carlos-Nango match!

00:24:51.550 --> 00:24:54.470
Carlos smiles as he fights an uphill battle.

00:24:54.470 --> 00:24:57.350
Robert and Yohko exchange an eerie glance.

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:59.980
But when the final round begins, with Nango in the lead,

00:24:59.980 --> 00:25:02.270
something happens that no one could have predicted!

00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:06.780
Now, as Joe is drawn to Carlos' unfathomable power,

00:25:06.780 --> 00:25:08.110
which way is tomorrow!?
